## Fixed design

[VERIFIED BY RUNNING CODE] The run used C3 only, the twelve fixed LRSWEEP C3
anchors and identical LOAO folds, model seed `V025_LEARNER/seed/1`
(`6407676579069309528`), the sealed `(64,64)` ReLU architecture, all sealed
Adam literals, and the route's current literal learning rate `1e-3`. Arm A
called LRSWEEP's full-batch C3 gradient aggregation directly. Its values at
updates 0, 100, 200, 300, 400, and 500 exactly reproduced the prior C3
`1e-3` cell.

[VERIFIED BY RUNNING CODE] The rule was applied at every destination cadence
`k = 100, 200, ..., 4000` to the immediately preceding interval `k-100 -> k`:

- objective relative absolute motion no greater than `0.01`;
- held-out level R2 absolute motion no greater than `0.01`;
- held-out within-group ordering absolute motion no greater than `0.005`;
- held-out top-1 absolute motion no greater than `0.005`.

All four checks had to pass together, with finite objective and parameters.
Arm B's checkpoint objective was evaluated on the complete training fold, not
on its last minibatch.

[VERIFIED BY RUNNING CODE] Arm B used batch size 256. For each LOAO fold, the
eleven training anchors were concatenated in LRSWEEP's fixed filename order.
